{"html":"<p>Rust's pitch — memory safety without a garbage collector — matters most where\nthere is no operating system to clean up after you.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-the-domain-demands\">What the domain demands</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Requirement</th>\n<th>Consequence</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>No heap</td>\n<td>A 64 KB RAM part cannot afford an allocator</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Deterministic timing</td>\n<td>An interrupt that arrives 200 µs late is a missed deadline</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>No hidden allocation</td>\n<td><code>Vec</code> growth in an ISR is a bug, not a slow path</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Provable absence of UB</td>\n<td>Certification bodies require it, not just tests</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Long support windows</td>\n<td>Firmware ships for 15 years</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The absence of a GC is not a performance argument here; it is a correctness\nargument. There is nowhere to run a collector.</p>\n<h2 id=\"who-runs-it\">Who runs it</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>System</th>\n<th>Detail</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Espressif (ESP32)</strong></td>\n<td>first-class Rust support via <code>esp-hal</code>; officially maintained, not a community fork</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Microsoft Azure Sphere</strong></td>\n<td>Rust supported for applications on the secured MCU platform</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Linux kernel</strong></td>\n<td>Rust in-tree since 6.1; real drivers, not just samples</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Ferrocene</strong></td>\n<td>a qualified Rust toolchain for ISO 26262 (automotive) and IEC 61508 (industrial) — certification is what unlocks safety-critical adoption</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>RTIC</strong></td>\n<td>a real-time concurrency framework whose interrupt priorities are checked at compile time</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Drone and robotics stacks</strong></td>\n<td>Rust in flight-controller components where a panic is a crash — literally</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"the-compile-time-guarantee-that-sells-it\">The compile-time guarantee that sells it</h2>\n<p>RTIC's trick: the borrow checker enforces that two interrupt handlers at\nconflicting priorities cannot access the same peripheral.</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"rust\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"rust\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">#[rtic</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">app(device </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> stm32l4xx_hal</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">pac, peripherals </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> true, dispatchers </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> [</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">TIM3</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">])]</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">mod</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> app</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> {</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">    use</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> stm32l4xx_hal</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">prelude</