ging.</strong> One tool, no vendor IDE.</li>\n<li><strong>Budget flash and RAM in CI.</strong> <code>cargo size --release</code> in the pipeline catches\nthe day someone pulls in <code>core::fmt</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"where-rust-is-the-wrong-answer\">Where Rust is the wrong answer</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>A part with no LLVM backend. If <code>rustc</code> cannot target it, the conversation ends.</li>\n<li>Teams with existing certified C code and no appetite for re-certification.</li>\n<li>Ultra-low-power parts where a 20 KB binary is already too big.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Build <code>blinky</code> for any Cortex-M board (or QEMU), then rewrite it against\n<code>embedded-hal</code> traits and compile the same function for a second chip. The moment\nthe identical driver code compiles for two different MCUs is the moment the\necosystem's design makes sense.</p>\n<p><strong>Next:</strong> <a href=\"06-web-and-wasm.md\">Web and WebAssembly</a></p>"}